language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_015_schurs_lemma: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Put n balls, labelled 1 to n, into 3 boxes so that for any triple of balls x, y, z with x + y = z, where x and y may be equal, not all three balls are in the same box. A solution exists if and only if n < 14.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_015_schurs_lemma.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_015_schurs_lemma.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_015_schurs_lemma_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_015_schurs_lemma.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_015_schurs_lemma_1.param -run-solver

$ n: number of balls, labelled 1 to n
given n : int
$ c: number of boxes
given c : int

$ balls[i]: box that ball i is put into, boxes numbered 1 to c, indices 1-based
find balls : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..c)

$ search hint: branch on the box of each ball
branching on [balls]

such that
$ for every pair x, y with x + y = z <= n, the balls x, y and z are not all in the same box
forAll x : int(1..n) . forAll y : int(1..n) . ((x + y <= n) -> !(balls[x] = balls[y] /\ balls[y] = balls[x+y]))
